  "id": "COMPOUND:19392 - PROTEIN:5845",
  "verbalization": "Islandicin 4-Methyl Ether is shown to have a target relationship with Macrophage scavenger receptor types I and II, which are subsequently targeted by two different compounds—2-(3,4-dihydroxyphenyl)-5,7-dihydroxy-8-[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxy-3-[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-[[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxymethyl]oxan-2-yl]oxychromen-4-one and 7-Hydroxy-6-(2-(R)-Hydroxy-3-Methylbut-3-Enyl)Coumarin. Both of these compounds are shown to target SNU1, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Islandicin 4-Methyl Ether may interact with SNU1. The evidence suggests that the interaction involves macrophage scavenger receptors, which are likely to play a role in the cellular response to the compound. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting the same downstream pathway supports the idea that the interaction is mediated through a shared biological process, possibly involving receptor activation or signaling pathways. The integration of these findings highlights the potential for Islandicin 4-Methyl Ether to influence SNU1 through a mechanism involving macrophage scavenger receptors, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
